  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/52ecfaaa72633fd76cca857b65ada4fb8238822bbe51fed4f913ecf41753e378.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $2$ units, so the distance equals $2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/59ec31381dd594b4219dd89dfff899d8d937bfff40b41280e21575c505a4feba.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/f7ed15e2eb21768de1db6e60694dcacdbcc9072f425170e990f1bb32295f9f46.png)\n\nThe point $(2,-1)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(4,-1)$ is at a distance of $4$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $4-2=2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
